course: dictionary
lesson: 996
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Boil is a word with more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. «A lollipop or boiled sweet is sugar syrup boiled until almost all the water is gone.» Here boiled means cooked, and the clue is sugar syrup and water going away.
explain: «A watched pot never boils» is a saying, not a real pot. Boil here means that time feels slower when you stare and wait. Always ask what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Boil can also be a noun, a thing you can have. A boil is a painful red swelling on the skin, full of pus. Look at the other words: a sentence about a sore, red arm is about a boil, not about water.
fact: Boil means a liquid gets so hot that it bubbles and turns into steam.
fact: Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius (212 degrees Fahrenheit) at sea level.
fact: A boil is a painful red swelling on the skin, full of pus.
fact: Boiled sweets are made from sugar syrup cooked until almost all the water is gone.
fact: Boiling water and steam can cause bad burns, so keep children away from the stove and turn pan handles inward.
exercise: «Coal, oil and gas power stations burn fuel to boil water into steam that spins turbines.» What does boil mean here? | *Heat water until it bubbles and turns into steam | A painful red spot on the skin | Burn the water until it is gone | Cook an egg in a pan
exercise: «A watched pot never boils» is a saying. What does it mean? | Watching a pot makes it heat up faster | Pots are never useful in a kitchen | Pots break if somebody looks at them | *Time feels slower when you stare and wait
exercise: Mia had a painful red swelling on her arm, full of pus. What is it called? | A sunburn | *A boil | A bruise | A blister on the foot
test: «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees, but it does not boil because of the huge pressure of the deep sea.» What stops the water from boiling? | The cold water | The salt in the sea | *The huge pressure of the deep sea | The darkness
test: In «It boils down to one rule: keep children away from the stove», what does boils down to mean? | It is boiling hot | The water is coming to the boil | It bubbles over the side | *The main point is
exam: «The click you hear when the kettle has boiled» tells you the water has reached boiling point. Which meaning of boil is used here? | *The water has bubbled and turned to steam | The kettle is broken and needs fixing | A painful swelling on the skin | Cooked food is ready to eat
